{"headword":"יָתַר","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>vb.</strong> remain over <strong>(</strong>NH <em>id.</em>; Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">יְתַר</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܝܺܬܰܪ</span> <em>id.</em>; Zinj. <span dir=\"rtl\">יתר</span> n. <em>rest, remainder;</em> Ethiopic ወተረ Assyrian [<em>atâru</em>], <em>remain over</em>, in der. conj., Dl<sup>HWB</sup>; in Sab. <span dir=\"rtl\">ותר</span> CIS <sup>iv, 15, 46, p. 77</sup>; especially n. <span dir=\"rtl\">ותר</span> as epithet of king = <em>noble one</em>, and as n.pr. <span dir=\"rtl\">ותרם</span> Mordt<sup>ZMG, 1876, 37, 292</sup> DHM<sup>ZMG, 1883, 15</sup> CIS<sup>iv, 10</sup>; Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">وَتَرَ</span> is <em>make single, make to be one</em>, or <em>an odd number</em><strong>)</strong>—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַיּוֹתֵר</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 15:15\" href=\"/I_Samuel.15.15\">1 S 15:15</a> <em>the remainder</em>†."}],"all_cited":true,"form":"Qal"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>be left over, remain over;</em> Pf. <span dir=\"rtl\">נוֹתַר</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 10:15\" href=\"/Exodus.10.15\">Ex 10:15</a> + 8 times, etc.; Impf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יִוָּתֵר</span> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 20:17\" href=\"/II_Kings.20.17\">2 K 20:17</a> + 2 times; <span dir=\"rtl\">יִוָּתֶ֥ר בָּ֑הּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 13:8\" href=\"/Zechariah.13.8\">Zc 13:8</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיִּוָּתֵר</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 32:25\" href=\"/Genesis.32.25\">Gn 32:25</a> + 2 times; <span dir=\"rtl\">וָאִוָּתֵר</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 19:10\" href=\"/I_Kings.19.10\">1 K 19:10</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 19:14\" href=\"/I_Kings.19.14\">14</a>, etc.; Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">נוֹתָר</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 2:26\" href=\"/I_Samuel.2.26\">1 S 2:26</a> + 17 times, <span dir=\"rtl\">נֹתָר</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 12:10\" href=\"/Exodus.12.10\">Ex 12:10</a>; fs. <span dir=\"rtl\">נוֹתֶ֫רֶת</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 2:3\" href=\"/Leviticus.2.3\">Lv 2:3</a> + 3 times; mpl. <span dir=\"rtl\">נוֹתָרִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 8:10\" href=\"/Judges.8.10\">Ju 8:10</a> + 24 times, etc.;—<em>be left over, remain</em> (<em>over</em>), abs. <a data-ref=\"Exodus 10:15\" href=\"/Exodus.10.15\">Ex 10:15</a> (J), <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:11\" href=\"/Joshua.11.11\">Jos 11:11</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 11:22\" href=\"/Joshua.11.22\">22</a> (D), <a data-ref=\"Judges 9:5\" href=\"/Judges.9.5\">Ju 9:5</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 1:8\" href=\"/Isaiah.1.8\">Is 1:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 30:17\" href=\"/Isaiah.30.17\">30:17</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 18:22\" href=\"/I_Kings.18.22\">1 K 18:22</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 20:17\" href=\"/II_Kings.20.17\">2 K 20:17</a> = <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 39:6\" href=\"/Isaiah.39.6\">Is 39:6</a>; sq. <span dir=\"rtl\">לְבַדּוֹ</span> <em>be left alone</em> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 32:25\" href=\"/Genesis.32.25\">Gn 32:25</a> (J), so <a data-ref=\"I Kings 19:10\" href=\"/I_Kings.19.10\">1 K 19:10</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 19:14\" href=\"/I_Kings.19.14\">14</a>; sq. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן</span> <em>be left from</em> (= <em>of</em>) <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 13:30\" href=\"/II_Samuel.13.30\">2 S 13:30</a> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 29:34\" href=\"/Exodus.29.34\">Ex 29:34</a> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 26:65\" href=\"/Numbers.26.65\">Nu 26:65</a> (both P), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 106:11\" href=\"/Psalms.106.11\">ψ 106:11</a>; pt. sq. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִן</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 8:10\" href=\"/Judges.8.10\">Ju 8:10</a> + 10 times P, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 9:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.9.20\">1 K 9:20</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 8:7\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.8.7\">2 Ch 8:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 14:16\" href=\"/Zechariah.14.16\">Zc 14:16</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 6:46\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.6.46\">1 Ch 6:46</a>; sq. <span dir=\"rtl\">לְ</span>, <em>be left</em> (<em>surviving</em>) <em>to</em>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 25:34\" href=\"/I_Samuel.25.34\">1 S 25:34</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 9:1\" hr